---
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
import Documentation from '../layouts/Documentation.astro';
import catalogue from '../../../../packages/contracts/components.json';
const layouts=['ProfilePageLayout','WorkspaceLayout','DashboardPageLayout','DetailPageLayout','ListViewTemplate','EdgeToEdgeLayout','ViewLayout','DashboardBand','SplitBand'];
---
<Documentation title="Page layouts"><main class="docs-catalogue"><h1>Choose the page geometry.</h1><p>Start with the outer frame, then the page template, then its organisms. Exactly one region owns vertical scrolling. Do not add padding around an edge-to-edge template.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Composition</th><th>Scroll owner</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Workspace</td><td>WorkspaceLayout → page template → organism</td><td>Main region</td></tr><tr><td>List</td><td>ListViewTemplate → TableCollection</td><td>Table body; toolbar stays above it</td></tr><tr><td>Dashboard</td><td>DashboardPageLayout → MetricStrip → ViewLayout → charts</td><td>Dashboard page</td></tr><tr><td>Full-bleed dashboard</td><td>EdgeToEdgeLayout → DashboardBand / SplitBand</td><td>Host page; no outer gutter</td></tr><tr><td>Entity detail</td><td>DetailPageLayout → properties / description / related table</td><td>Detail body beneath header and tabs</td></tr></tbody></table><nav class="docs-index" aria-label="Layout recipes">{catalogue.filter(item=>layouts.includes(item.name)).map(item=><a href={`${base}/components/${item.name}/`}><strong>{item.name}</strong><span>{item.purpose}</span></a>)}</nav><h2>Name organisms by their function</h2><p>MetricStrip replaces the AI-specific KPI row name; MetricGrid names the responsive subject metric grid. TableCollection names the complete DataView composition. AnalyticsChart and DashboardChart distinguish the full renderer from the chart-and-legend composition. The old import paths remain migration adapters.</p><p>ForecastTable and EddyPanel are also organisms. Keep calculations and services outside their presentation contracts.</p></main></Documentation>
